  <running_head>ARTICULORUM.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">II. Nomen proprium, junctum ap-</l>
    <l n="2">pellativo cum Articulo, ipsum Articulo</l>
    <l n="3">caret. ut: Παῦλος ὁ Ἀπόστολος.</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">III. Cùm duo Nomina substantiva,</l>
    <l n="5">aut substantivum cum adjectivo, eâdem</l>
    <l n="6">constructione junguntur, utrumque</l>
    <l n="7">nonnunquam Articulo insignitur. ut:</l>
    <l n="8">ὁμιλος ταχχήματα.</l>
    <l n="9">ὁ πλούσιος ὁ ονειροπόλης.</l>
    <l n="10" para="true">IV. Cùm inter duo Nomina sub-</l>
    <l n="11">stantiva, aut inter substantivum &amp; ad-</l>
    <l n="12">jectivum, intercedit</l>
    <l n="13">Verbum, aut sub-</l>
    <l n="14">intelligitur: vel utrumque Articulum</l>
    <l n="15">habet; vel id tantùm, quod subjecti lo-</l>
    <l n="16">cum tenet. ut:</l>
    <l n="17">τὸ πνεῦμά ἐστι τὸ ζωοποιῶν.</l>
    <l n="18">Θεὸς ἦν ὁ Λόγος.</l>
    <l n="19">πνεῦμα ὁ Θεός.</l>
    <l n="20" para="true">V. Articulus sinè casu respondente,</l>
    <l n="21">prepositus genitivo substantivi, posses-</l>
    <l n="22">sionem aut effectum significat: servit-</l>
    <l n="23">que eleganti brevitati; subaudito con-</l>
    <l n="24">veniente aliquo Substantivo aut Participio. ut:</l>
    <l n="25">μεγαλῶν χάρις ἐμπιπλαμένη οἱ γονέων διαθήκων.</l>
    <l n="26">Τὰ τῶν Φίλων, καινά.</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Greek passages are partly illegible in the scan; transcription of Greek is approximate. Marked words are doubtful.</notes>
